* 2026-10-29 - oxedions, Claude - [haproxy] Fix backend resources with several servers (invalid configuration, all servers on one line), fix backend/frontend with empty parameters (role crash, README example), open frontends ports in the firewall (OS firewall task files never existed), rebuild http_load_balancer on HAProxy native redir (health checks now target real servers so dead servers are no longer used, path and query string kept, 302 instead of 301, local_ports_first is now ignored), remove broken undocumented http_load_balancer_v2. Default global settings now portable: stats socket in /var/lib/haproxy, created by the role (HAProxy did not start where /run/haproxy does not exist, like RHEL 10), logs to journald (log stdout, works with chroot), no daemon nor RHEL only PROFILE=SYSTEM ciphers. Validate configuration with haproxy -c before install, reload instead of restart, remove dead httpd code and exploration notes, document haproxy_resources_raw and haproxy_enable_ip_nonlocal_bind.
* 2026-10-28 - oxedions, Claude - [grafana] BREAKING: role rewritten and simplified (3.0.0), variables of previous versions are rejected with a clear message (migration table in README). grafana.ini options are now set through a single grafana_configuration dictionary, admin account through grafana_admin_user/grafana_admin_password, LDAP through raw grafana_ldap_configuration. Datasources and dashboards are now provisioned with files (no more HTTP API calls nor community.grafana dependency, works with --skip-tags service). Fix admin password enforcement (grafana-cli reset the password of another database, password visible in process list), fix local dashboards never loaded, fix --tags handling and role hanging with --skip-tags service, start Grafana only once configured. Removed API keys (removed from Grafana 12), direct OSS packages install, socket mode, low ports capability, uid/gid forcing. README documents Grafana repositories per distribution (RHEL 10 AppStream ships Grafana 10.2, openSUSE Leap 16 ships Grafana 12).
